# Roadmap Localization Workflow

When asked to add new roadmap updates to translation files:

- Source of truth is `_roadmap.json` (latest entries at top).
- Target files are `_roadmap_de.json`, `_roadmap_es.json`, `_roadmap_fr.json`.
- Add the same new entries in the same order to each target file.
- Keep metadata identical to source entry: `update`, `title` number, `date`, `oculus`, `steam`.
- Translate only:
  - Text in the heading line inside `<align=center>...`
  - The first paragraph before "See build notes..." (or equivalent localized line)
- Preserve all color tags exactly as in source (same tags, same hex values, same placement).
- From "See build notes..." onward, reuse the existing localized tail from that file's `update 15` block verbatim.
- Do not rewrite or normalize old entries unless explicitly requested.
- After edits, verify top-of-file entries in all target files for:
  - Correct ordering
  - Correct color tag integrity
  - Correct link fields
  - Tail text copied from that locale's `update 15`
